## 🚀 Problem Statement

Many real-world graph use-cases require knowing whether a graph is acyclic (a DAG):

- Dependency resolution (npm, gradle, CMake itself) requires DAG validation
- Task scheduling and topological sort require no cycles
- Deadlock detection in OS modeling requires cycle detection

CinderPeak supports both **directed** and **undirected** graphs, but provides **no cycle detection algorithm**. A user building a dependency resolver on top of CinderPeak has no way to validate that their graph is acyclic before running topological sort.

## ✅ Proposed Solution

### `src/algorithms/CycleDetection.hpp`

```cpp
// src/algorithms/CycleDetection.hpp
#pragma once
#include <unordered_map>
#include <unordered_set>
#include "CinderPeak.hpp"

namespace CinderPeak {

// DFS-based cycle detection for DIRECTED graphs (3-color algorithm)
template <typename V, typename E>
bool has_cycle_directed(const CinderGraph<V, E>& graph) {
    enum Color { WHITE, GRAY, BLACK };
    std::unordered_map<V, Color> color;
    for (const auto& v : graph.vertices()) color[v] = WHITE;

    std::function<bool(const V&)> dfs = [&](const V& u) -> bool {
        color[u] = GRAY;
        for (const auto& [v, _] : graph.neighbors(u)) {
            if (color[v] == GRAY) return true;  // back edge = cycle
            if (color[v] == WHITE && dfs(v)) return true;
        }
        color[u] = BLACK;
        return false;
    };

    for (const auto& v : graph.vertices()) {
        if (color[v] == WHITE && dfs(v)) return true;
    }
    return false;
}

// Union-Find cycle detection for UNDIRECTED graphs
template <typename V, typename E>
bool has_cycle_undirected(const CinderGraph<V, E>& graph) {
    std::unordered_map<V, V> parent;
    for (const auto& v : graph.vertices()) parent[v] = v;

    std::function<V(const V&)> find = [&](const V& x) -> V {
        if (parent[x] != x) parent[x] = find(parent[x]);
        return parent[x];
    };

    for (const auto& [u, neighbors] : graph.adjacency()) {
        for (const auto& [v, _] : neighbors) {
            V pu = find(u), pv = find(v);
            if (pu == pv) return true;
            parent[pu] = pv;
        }
    }
    return false;
}

// Unified API — auto-detects graph type
template <typename V, typename E>
bool has_cycle(const CinderGraph<V, E>& graph) {
    return graph.isDirected()
        ? has_cycle_directed(graph)
        : has_cycle_undirected(graph);
}

} // namespace CinderPeak
```

### GTest file `tests/test_cycle_detection.cpp`

```cpp
TEST(CycleDetectionTest, DirectedCyclicGraph) {
    CinderPeak::CinderGraph<int, int> g(directed_opts);
    g.addVertex(1); g.addVertex(2); g.addVertex(3);
    g.addEdge(1, 2, 0); g.addEdge(2, 3, 0); g.addEdge(3, 1, 0);
    EXPECT_TRUE(CinderPeak::has_cycle(g));
}

TEST(CycleDetectionTest, DirectedAcyclicGraph) {
    CinderPeak::CinderGraph<int, int> g(directed_opts);
    g.addVertex(1); g.addVertex(2); g.addVertex(3);
    g.addEdge(1, 2, 0); g.addEdge(2, 3, 0);
    EXPECT_FALSE(CinderPeak::has_cycle(g));
}
```

