## Summary

CinderPeak has no graph traversal algorithms. BFS and DFS are the foundational building blocks from which most other graph algorithms (connected components, cycle detection, topological sort, bipartite checking) are derived. Without them, users must write raw traversal logic from scratch for every use case.

## Problem

- There are no `bfs()` or `dfs()` functions in `src/`.
- Graph traversal is the most frequently needed primitive when working with any graph library.
- The absence of traversal algorithms means users cannot: find connected components, detect cycles, check reachability, or build more complex algorithms on top of the library.
- A visitor-pattern-based design would make both algorithms extensible — users can inject custom logic at each vertex visit without modifying library code.

## Proposed Solution

**`src/algorithms/traversal.hpp`:**
```cpp
#pragma once
#include <queue>
#include <stack>
#include <unordered_set>
#include <functional>
#include "CinderPeak.hpp"

namespace CinderPeak {

/**
 * Visitor interface: called on each vertex during traversal.
 * Return false to stop traversal early.
 */
template <typename V>
using VertexVisitor = std::function<bool(const V&)>;

template <typename V, typename E>
void bfs(const CinderGraph<V, E>& graph, const V& source, VertexVisitor<V> visitor) {
    std::unordered_set<V> visited;
    std::queue<V> q;
    q.push(source);
    visited.insert(source);
    while (!q.empty()) {
        V u = q.front(); q.pop();
        if (!visitor(u)) return;
        for (auto& [v, _] : graph.neighbors(u)) {
            if (!visited.count(v)) {
                visited.insert(v);
                q.push(v);
            }
        }
    }
}

template <typename V, typename E>
void dfs(const CinderGraph<V, E>& graph, const V& source, VertexVisitor<V> visitor) {
    std::unordered_set<V> visited;
    std::stack<V> s;
    s.push(source);
    while (!s.empty()) {
        V u = s.top(); s.pop();
        if (visited.count(u)) continue;
        visited.insert(u);
        if (!visitor(u)) return;
        for (auto& [v, _] : graph.neighbors(u)) {
            if (!visited.count(v)) s.push(v);
        }
    }
}

/** Returns all vertices reachable from source */
template <typename V, typename E>
std::vector<V> reachableFrom(const CinderGraph<V, E>& graph, const V& source) {
    std::vector<V> result;
    bfs(graph, source, [&](const V& v) { result.push_back(v); return true; });
    return result;
}

} // namespace CinderPeak
```

